The most interesting failure here is the gap between what the participant *knows* (articulated brilliantly in the debrief) and what they *do* (in the roleplay). This gap is itself a form of emotional intelligence—the ability to recognize one's own limitations. But it also suggests the participant may be more comfortable analyzing emotional dynamics than inhabiting them with genuine uncertainty.

